%% W3D3 — Hybrid Search & Reranking — Request Flow
%% Shows parallel retrieval, RRF fusion, cross-encoder reranking, and fallback path
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant App as Application
    participant Dispatcher as Query Dispatcher
    participant BM25 as BM25 Index
    participant VectorDB as Vector Store
    participant Fusion as RRF Fusion
    participant Reranker as Cross-Encoder Reranker
    participant LLM as Language Model

    User->>App: Submit query string
    App->>Dispatcher: Forward raw query
    Note over Dispatcher: Fan-out both retrievers in parallel
    Dispatcher->>BM25: Sparse retrieval - top-100
    Dispatcher->>VectorDB: Dense ANN retrieval - top-100
    BM25-->>Dispatcher: Ranked list A with BM25 scores
    VectorDB-->>Dispatcher: Ranked list B with cosine scores
    Dispatcher->>Fusion: Merge lists A and B
    Fusion->>Fusion: Compute RRF score per document
    Note over Fusion: score = sum(1 / (60 + rank)) across lists
    Fusion-->>Dispatcher: Fused top-50 candidates
    alt Reranker available
        Dispatcher->>Reranker: Score top-50 with original query
        Note over Reranker: Cross-encoder sees query + doc jointly
        Reranker-->>Dispatcher: Reranked top-10 with relevance scores
        Dispatcher-->>App: Top-5 documents by rerank score
    else Reranker unavailable - fallback
        Note over Dispatcher: Degraded mode - use RRF results directly
        Dispatcher-->>App: Top-5 documents by RRF score
    end
    App->>LLM: Query + retrieved context window
    LLM-->>App: Generated answer with citations
    App-->>User: Final response
